> **To send data from JS to android**

**(In the android)**

1. Update the following setting on the webview element:

   ```
   webview.addJavascriptInterface(WebAppInterface(this), "KwikIDNativeInterface")
   ```

2. Here "KwikIDNativeInterface" is the custom even name and "WebAppInterface(this)" is the custom interface with a custom function. ([Sample file](https://bitbucket.org/team360noscope/native_android_user_webview/src/2816b191e9c75f481d625b9c7a89bce5412ca301/app/src/main/java/com/example/webview_app/Interfaces/WebAppInterface.kt))

**(In the JS)**

1. Add the following code to the index.html:

   ```
    window.callNativeFunction = (type, params) => {
           console.log("window.callNativeFunction = ", type, params);
           switch (type) {
             case "WEB_ACTION":
               KwikIDNativeInterface.perfromWebAction(params);
               break;
             default:
               break;
           }
         };
   ```

2. Call the function ("callNativeFunction") from any component as per the need.  
   Eg:

   ```
   window["callNativeFunction"]("WEB_ACTION", JSON.stringify({"data":"anything"}));
   ```

> **To send data from android to JS**

**(In the Android)**

1. Calling the following function on the webview element with 'javascript' tag as shown below: (this method should be only called in UI Thread) :

   ```
   val responseData = JSONObject()
   responseData.put("type", "RESPONSE_FROM_NATIVE")
   responseData.put("request", JSONObject(data))
   
   runOnUiThread {
       webview.loadUrl("javascript:dataFromNative('$responseData')");
   }
   ```

2. Here "dataFromNative" is the custom function name which should be matched at the JS end as well.

**(In the JS)**

1. Add the following function in the index.html, this function is dispatching global event.

   ```
   function dataFromNative(data) {
           let nativeData = JSON.parse(data);
           switch (nativeData.type) {
             case "RESPONSE_FROM_NATIVE":
               dispatchEvent(
                 new CustomEvent("RESPONSE_FROM_NATIVE", {
                   detail: {
                     data: nativeData,
                     time: new Date()
                   },
                   bubbles: true,
                   cancelable: true
                 })
               );
               break;
   
             default:
               break;
           }
         }
   ```

2. To listen the above event following method can be used

   ```
   window.addEventListener("RESPONSE_FROM_NATIVE", (message) => {
           console.log("Message from RESPONSE_FROM_NATIVE: ", message, message["detail"]); }
   ```

